From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pallavi Singh <palsing@nvidia.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Mar 2026 19:47:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 234/243] NVIDIA: SAUCE: PCI/MSI: Skip EP register access when
 device is disconnected

When a PCIe EP is disconnected (hot unplug or link down), the
device is marked disconnected but teardown still runs and
free_irq() is called. That triggers the IRQ chip mask path.

pci_msi_update_mask(): Reached as free_irq() -> pci_msi_mask_irq()
-> __pci_msi_mask_desc() -> pci_msi_mask() -> pci_msi_update_mask().
Writes the MSI Mask register in config space. Add
pci_dev_is_disconnected() to skip lock, in-memory mask update,
and config write when the device is disconnected.

pci_msix_mask() and pci_msix_unmask(): Reached as free_irq() ->
pci_msi_mask_irq() -> __pci_msi_mask_desc() -> pci_msix_mask() or
pci_msix_unmask(). They read/write the MSI-X vector table in PCIe
BAR (MMIO space). Add pci_dev_is_disconnected() to skip MMIO
access when the device is disconnected.

__pci_restore_msi_state(): Called to restore MSI state (e.g.
resume or error recovery). Writes config space and calls
pci_msi_update_mask(). Add pci_dev_is_disconnected() next to
msi_enabled check to skip restore when device is disconnected.

__pci_restore_msix_state(): Called to restore MSI-X state. Writes
config and MSI-X table MMIO. Add pci_dev_is_disconnected() next to
msix_enabled check to skip restore when device is disconnected.

Bug 5872237

